==Latin==

===Conjunction===
{{head|la|conjunction}}

# [[or]]
#: ''Marcus videbit ludos [[aut]] dormiet.''
#:: Marcus will watch the games <u>or</u> sleep.
#: ''[[aut|Aut]] caesar, [[aut]] nihil.''
#:: <u>Either</u> caesar <u>or</u> nothing (''figuratively:'' all or nothing)
#: ''[[aut|Aut]] disce [[aut]] discede.''
#:: <u>Either</u> learn <u>or</u> go away.

====Usage notes====
* This word is used in pairs (''[[aut]]'' ... ''[[aut]]'') to mean "{{term|either}}....{{term|or}}".
* Unlike {{term|vel|lang=la}}, this word implies an exclusive "or", i.e., one option or the other, but not both.<br>(see similiar distinction in Polish: "[[albo]]" and "[[lub]]")

